<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sergius of Radonezh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1314–1392</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sergius of Radonezh was a Russian monk who founded the Trinity Monastery north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> around the 1340s and became the most venerated saint of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. He revived communal monastic life, and his disciples founded dozens of monasteries across the northern forests. Tradition holds that he blessed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dmitry-donskoy">Dmitry Donskoy</a> before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kulikovo">Battle of Kulikovo</a> in 1380; his monastery became one of the great religious and landowning centres of Muscovy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sergius-of-radonezh.jpg" alt="Sergius of Radonezh" width="320" height="500" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sergius_of_Radonezh_vita_icon_(17_c.,_Yaroslavl_museum)_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
